@@ ============================================================
@@ σRf — propagation of uncertainty through a composite function
@@ of one variable.
@@
@@ Input:  'f(x)' X, where f is an expression of the name x, and X
@@         its value a±σb, with or without units.
@@ Output: f(X) as Y±σu.
@@ Unlike evaluating f on X directly, the variable is counted once,
@@ however often it appears: 'x-x' gives 0±σ0, and
@@ '(x-1)·(x-2)·(x-3)' the uncertainty of the function, not of
@@ its three factors taken as independent.
@@ Method: σRFxjxi with one variable (central differences).
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → fx xv
  «
    'fx' Rcl { x 'x1' } Where
    xv ⓁσRFxjxi
  »
»
